{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "זאת חקת התורה", :translit "zot chukat ha-torah", :gloss "this is the statute of the Torah"} {:he "חוקת התורה", :translit "chukat ha-torah", :gloss "statute of the Torah"} {:he "לבהרימכם את חלבו ממנו", :translit "le-harimchem et chelbo mimenu", :gloss "when you raise up its fat from upon it"} {:he "לא ניתנה תורה אלא לאוכלי המן", :translit "lo nittnah torah ela le-ochlei ha-man", :gloss "the Torah was given only to eaters of the manna"} {:he "שנייה לה לאוכלי תרומה", :translit "sheniyah lah le-ochlei terumah", :gloss "secondarily to it, to eaters of terumah"} {:he "תרומה לכהן עם הארץ", :translit "terumah le-kohen am ha-aretz", :gloss "terumah to an ignoramus priest"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Juxtaposition (semikhut): חקת התורה placed near לבהרימם את חלבו ממנו at end of prior section"}], :frame {:text "The phrase לא ניתנה תורה אלא לאוכלי המן is found in the Talmud: the Israelites were commanded regarding the manna before they received the Torah, teaching that Torah was given only to those who ate the manna (Yoma 75b). Separately, the rule that terumah may not be given to an עם הארץ is addressed in tractate Chullin, where an am ha-aretz is deemed suspect regarding purity laws (Chullin 4a–b). The Ba'al HaTurim links these two traditions through the juxtaposition of sections.", :sources ["Yoma 75b" "Chullin 4a"]}} {:quotes [{:he "לא תחללו", :translit "lo techalelu", :gloss "you shall not profane"} {:he "חוקת התורה", :translit "chukat ha-torah", :gloss "statute of the Torah"} {:he "ת\"ח שחוטא הוא חילול השם", :translit "t\"ch she-choteh hu chillul ha-shem", :gloss "a scholar who sins is a profanation of the Name"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Juxtaposition (semikhut): לא תחללו from prior verse placed adjacent to חקת התורה in this verse"}], :frame {:text "The concept that a Torah scholar's sin constitutes chillul Hashem appears in the Talmud's discussion of profaning the divine Name, where it is stated that a scholar must be especially scrupulous, for his transgression is judged as a desecration (Yoma 86a).", :sources ["Yoma 86a"]}} {:quotes [{:he "ולא תמותו", :translit "ve-lo tamutu", :gloss "and you shall not die"} {:he "חקת התורה", :translit "chukat ha-torah", :gloss "statute of the Torah"} {:he "עץ חיים היא למחזיקים בה", :translit "etz chayim hi le-machazikim bah", :gloss "she is a tree of life to those who hold fast to her"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Juxtaposition (semikhut): ולא תמותו from prior verse placed adjacent to חקת התורה in this verse; supported by verse citation"}], :frame {:text "The verse עץ חיים היא למחזיקים בה describes Torah as a tree of life to those who grasp it (Proverbs 3:18). The Ba'al HaTurim reads this as explaining why the juxtaposition of 'you shall not die' with 'the statute of the Torah' is apt: holding fast to Torah is itself associated with life.", :sources ["Proverbs 3:18"]}} {:quotes [{:he "פרה אדומה", :translit "parah adumah", :gloss "red heifer"} {:he "זה על עון עגל", :translit "zeh al avon eglah", :gloss "this is upon the sin of the calf"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "פרה אדומה", :b "זה על עון עגל"}], :frame {:text "The tradition that the red heifer atones for the sin of the golden calf is found in the Midrash: God said, 'Let the mother come and clean up the filth of her child' — the red heifer atoning for the red calf that Israel made (Numbers Rabbah 19:8). The phrase זה על עון עגל encodes this connection in gematria.", :sources ["Numbers Rabbah 19:8"]}} {:quotes [{:he "לא עלה עליה על", :translit "lo alah aleiha al", :gloss "no yoke has come upon it, yoke"} {:he "על", :translit "al", :gloss "yoke / upon"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Plene/defective spelling: על written chaser (without vav) at Numbers 19:2"}], :frame {:text "The word על appears in the phrase describing the red heifer that no yoke has come upon it (Numbers 19:2). The Ba'al HaTurim notes the defective spelling and derives that the disqualification extends beyond actual yoking: even merely mounting the animal invalidates it.", :sources ["Numbers 19:2"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Juxtaposition (semikhut): חקת התורה placed near לבהרימם את חלבו ממנו at end of prior section", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Juxtaposition (semikhut): לא תחללו from prior verse placed adjacent to חקת התורה in this verse", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Juxtaposition (semikhut): ולא תמותו from prior verse placed adjacent to חקת התורה in this verse; supported by verse citation", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :gematria, :a "פרה אדומה", :a-value 341, :b "זה על עון עגל", :b-value 341, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? true} {:kind :other, :note "Plene/defective spelling: על written chaser (without vav) at Numbers 19:2", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:30:13.533142207Z", :model "glm-5.2"}